add('# Corrected-v2 finalization evidence');add();add('Local, uncommitted validation package. Historical-only model fitting; no PostgreSQL/S3 writes or Transformer/RL integration. The completed full reference used the preserved pre-gap identity bundle. This corrected identity candidate has medium validation; final full validation is pending an explicit exception to the original ONE-run limit.');add()
add('## Version and runtime contract');add();add('`legacy-v2r2` and `corrected-v1` retain frozen v1/v2 assets. `corrected-v2` explicitly selects v3. Older defaults remain for compatibility; `config/corrected-v2.yaml` selects the new contract. The external interface is documented in `docs/corrected-v2-contract.md`.');add()
add('## Medium overactivity audit and mechanism fixes');add();add('The first medium candidate emitted 34,737 events: 34,415 new-application rows and 322 carried rows. First-seven-day events/application were 8.3822 versus the unchanged weekday-adjusted Phase 2 benchmark of 7.1375 (+17.4%). Repeated-substage counts were 2.1605 versus 1.4286 per application. Eventful application-days stayed close to history, identifying within-session overactivity. The candidate was rejected.');add();add('The natural cause-specific law censored PTP and then ran an independent PTP clock. Its competing-risk assumptions inflated repeated AIP/journey paths. The replacement models mutually exclusive next journey/eligible-terminal outcomes. Missing-prerequisite terminal mass remains inactive; guards are unchanged. Returning-customer history does not populate the new application\'s prerequisite flags. Separate historically fitted returning/new pools correct the population mixture.');add();add('Supported bursts contributed 893 same-time extra new rows in the rejected candidate, insufficient to explain the excess. Stage/global backoff accounted for 266 of 44,187 natural-law evaluations (<1%). Cached episode scheduling and WAIT segmentation tests exclude repeated polling redraws. No global event multiplier, probability scaling, forced loops, or jitter was introduced.');add();add('The accepted medium has 28,679 rows: 28,405 new and 274 carried, 4,096 arrivals, 13,007 carries, 45 carried applications active, 2,263 PTP, and 13,013 exact expiries. The final carry fix leaves every new Gold row and stochastic key identical to the preceding medium. Matched Friday/depth activity is 34 versus 47.86 expected, inside the 31.22–64.50 predictive interval.');add()
add('## Equal-age new application comparisons');add();add('The same Phase 2 population is independently reconstructed: 578,324 eligible events and 81,416 applications. Each horizon requires complete observation to that age. Weekday adjustment uses the simulated cohort distribution; no late arrivals with incomplete follow-up enter these comparisons.');add()
