add('## PTP eligibility audit');add();add('Mature March: 44,125 applications; 29,582 with eligible observed AIP; 55,199 eligible AIP episodes; 23,731 eligible PTP episodes. Raw PTP includes 4,335 outcomes without a strictly observed eligible prerequisite sequence. Conditional audit before changing runtime PTP found >7pp frozen young-age CDF errors in both March and April, outside application-cluster uncertainty, and an unsupported late-age global fallback predicting ~62.7% despite zero observed late eligible outcomes. The declared materiality threshold was >5pp conditional error with matching risk competition and uncertainty.');add();add('The preserved pre-gap full-reference eligible-episode young-age CDF is 0.6104 at 300s and 0.6916 at one day, versus historical March/April 0.6211/0.6139 and 0.6995/0.7086. Frozen hazard predicted 0.5424 at 300s and 0.6315 at one day. Late-age simulated eligible episodes have zero PTP, consistent with history. Frozen PTP CSV/donor/manifest files remain byte-identical. Corrected-v2 replaces the independent clock with the joint competing law; no terminal transition is allowed without current-application guards. Raw and observable PTP results are both reported above. Same-time canonical prerequisites explain the small difference between strict-timestamp and executable-order eligibility.');add()
add('## Namespace, external agent and recovery');add();add('Same seed/namespace with different operational run IDs produces identical logical Gold outcomes, including SEND/WAIT and event-name sampling. Different namespaces produce distinct realizations; mismatch is rejected before mutation/recovery. Namespace is persisted in runtime state, checkpoint, run manifest and summary. The medium tail-isolation comparison also proves all 28,405 new Gold rows and cumulative stochastic keys unchanged across operational runs.');add();add('`ExternalAgentSession.observe()` returns only current identifiers, simulated time and customer-scoped Gold-column history through that time. `decide(EnvironmentAction.send(...), next_decision_time)` or `decide(EnvironmentAction.wait(), next_decision_time)` advances organic and pending effects to the caller boundary. Multiple intraday decisions and overnight advances are supported; midnight adds no decision. Separate operator audit is not agent input. Generic core calendar bounds are configurable. Future observation leakage tests pass; pending queue/probabilities never enter observations. Crash-injection recovery tests cover all three commit boundaries, and WAIT segmentation includes carried applications.');add()
add('## Current candidate medium run' if args.medium_candidate else '## Final full-May run');add();add('```json');add(json.dumps(inv,indent=2));add('```');add();add('Seed 20260502; stochastic namespace `corrected-v2-reference-20260502`; operational run ID differs. Day 16 reopened the persisted runner. All 31 daily commit/checkpoint hash links, ownership, exact expiry removals, terminal ordering including ties, and pending boundary clocks are independently checked. No combined historical export or PostgreSQL load was required.');add()
add('## Validation, storage and compatibility');add();add('Full pytest: see `gap-outcome-full-pytest.log`: 90 passed. Focused empirical/contract and artifact-schema tests also pass. Artifact validation covers 31 declared runtime inputs, hashes and required schema. All 58 frozen v1/v2 file hashes remain unchanged. Focused May1 replay matches all three protected daily hashes for both legacy-v2r2 and corrected-v1; the accepted legacy combined SHA remains `7c81a5849d91ad139624bbdba3f9b955f6eba76819b773781acc231f98a4d037`. No additional full legacy run was needed. `git diff --check` passes.');add();add('All important artifacts, reports and run partitions remain on persistent root storage; no instance-store mount or destructive initialization was used. Final local package includes the v3 bundle, run summaries, fidelity evidence, source/code inventory and checksums. Accepted V2r2 S3/PostgreSQL data were untouched.');add()
add('## Known limitations and readiness');add();add('The primary Wednesday carry benchmark remains above the weekday/depth benchmark. Rare tail rates have substantial uncertainty; the carry predictive interval uses a normal cluster-sandwich approximation. Late gaps >24h remain low. Raw PTP is lower because current-application prerequisite observations are incomplete; guards remain authoritative. Returning status means an observed prior March-April lifecycle, not necessarily a first-ever customer otherwise. April was used for validation/model selection. Campaign response assets remain observational.');add()
